1
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:12,920
Go ahead and gallop away, okay?

2
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:22,280
Someone's calling out to you.

3
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:24,660
Over there is Kameari.

4
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:28,020
Well, I'm sure it's Kameari.

5
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:33,040
Everyone, come on over to our town!

6
00:00:34,020 --> 00:00:34,660
Thank you.

7
00:01:06,020 --> 00:01:07,040
Here, I'm returning these.

8
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:12,040
What do you mean,
sending it back without even looking at it?

9
00:01:12,040 --> 00:01:17,600
None of the marriage proposals the Chief has brought
me so far have had a single decent woman in them.

10
00:01:17,600 --> 00:01:18,980
No, thank you.

11
00:01:19,820 --> 00:01:23,500
You idiot,
you're in no position to be so picky!

12
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:30,200
Listen, a woman generous enough to agree to
a meeting with you may never show up again!

13
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:31,740
I refuse.

14
00:01:31,740 --> 00:01:34,720
I have no intention of getting
married for the time being.

15
00:01:36,020 --> 00:01:39,040
I've made up my mind that my
marriage will be a love match.

16
00:01:39,040 --> 00:01:44,640
Do you really think there's some weirdo
who'd want a love marriage with a man like you?

17
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:45,960
Of course.

18
00:01:45,960 --> 00:01:48,440
Chief, you really don't get it at all.

19
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:51,020
Even if I don't look like it,
I'm quite popular, you know.

20
00:01:55,040 --> 00:01:56,840
You, popular with women?

21
00:01:59,540 --> 00:02:00,900
Don't joke around.

22
00:02:00,900 --> 00:02:05,260
Stories about you dating
or going out with a woman,

23
00:02:06,520 --> 00:02:09,860
I've never heard a single
word of that until now!

24
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:11,800
What are you talking about?

25
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:15,100
I've finally settled down recently.

26
00:02:15,580 --> 00:02:19,900
Ten years ago,
the women were so pushy, so pushy,

27
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:23,200
"Ryo-chan, if you don't marry, you'll die!"

28
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:27,740
they even said they wanted
to have Ryo-san's baby.

29
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:31,420
And who might those people be, Ryotsu-kun?

30
00:02:31,420 --> 00:02:35,540
Akemi-chan from Kanaichi-cho,
or Naomi-chan from Shin-Koiwa,

31
00:02:36,020 --> 00:02:37,300
Isn't that the big sister from Kamiya?!

32
00:02:37,480 --> 00:02:40,300
Lines like that are what any
hostess says to every customer.

33
00:02:40,300 --> 00:02:42,200
You've got to be kidding me.

34
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:45,560
Excuse me, Chief, do you have a moment?

35
00:02:45,900 --> 00:02:46,680
What is it?

36
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:49,020
Senpai, there's a visitor for you.

37
00:02:49,020 --> 00:02:49,760
For me?

38
00:02:53,140 --> 00:02:54,020
Dad!

39
00:02:54,620 --> 00:02:56,140
I missed you so much!

40
00:02:57,040 --> 00:02:57,920
Dad.

41
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:00,400
Dad?

42
00:03:01,120 --> 00:03:04,220
No way, I don't know you, got it?

43
00:03:04,220 --> 00:03:05,200
Dad!

44
00:03:06,020 --> 00:03:07,960
Watch it! Hey, get off me!

45
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:08,840
*Thud!*

46
00:03:09,780 --> 00:03:10,120
Are you all right?

47
00:03:11,700 --> 00:03:15,360
Ryo-chan, what do you think you're doing to
your own child who came all this way to visit?

48
00:03:18,540 --> 00:03:19,740
Poor thing.

49
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:25,220
Hey, what do you think you're doing?

50
00:03:25,220 --> 00:03:28,220
I'd say a first-class 94, F-cup.

51
00:03:29,020 --> 00:03:31,320
Look at you, acting smart with me.

52
00:03:31,320 --> 00:03:32,300
You brat!

53
00:03:38,740 --> 00:03:40,300
Pulling a dirty trick like that!

54
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:43,060
There's no such thing as dirty tricks in a fight,
you know.

55
00:03:43,060 --> 00:03:43,980
Stop it.

56
00:03:43,980 --> 00:03:46,340
That's childish of you, you know.

57
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:48,560
Hey, you! I'll hit you right in the nose!

58
00:03:50,040 --> 00:03:52,820
You're exactly like Ryotsu in every way.

59
00:03:52,940 --> 00:03:55,728
Your sneakiness, your lecherous side,

60
00:03:55,778 --> 00:03:57,340
even your eyebrows are identical.

61
00:03:57,680 --> 00:04:00,680
Even his name is Kankichiro, this boy.

62
00:04:00,980 --> 00:04:01,620
What!?

63
00:04:02,300 --> 00:04:03,920
Kankichiro!?

64
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,240
Mom told me.

65
00:04:07,380 --> 00:04:10,540
She said my name was taken from Dad's name.

66
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:13,360
Kankichi, so Kankichiro

67
00:04:13,980 --> 00:04:16,600
This guy could really be Ryotsu's son.

68
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:22,140
Well then, Kankichiro,
could you tell us the whole story?

69
00:04:22,760 --> 00:04:23,120
Yeah.

70
00:04:24,320 --> 00:04:29,580
I was always told by Mom that
Dad died when he was a baby.

71
00:04:30,100 --> 00:04:34,840
But a week ago, Mom died in a car accident.

72
00:04:34,840 --> 00:04:39,800
Before she died, she took my hand

73
00:04:39,800 --> 00:04:42,800
and said there's something
I have to tell you.

74
00:04:43,220 --> 00:04:45,620
Dad is actually alive.

75
00:04:50,920 --> 00:04:54,620
Your daddy is a police officer

76
00:04:55,100 --> 00:04:57,960
at the Kameari Park police box named Kankichi Ryotsu,
that's what I was told.

77
00:04:59,120 --> 00:05:01,300
But Mom fell for him on her own,

78
00:05:01,300 --> 00:05:03,120
and had you in secret.

79
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:06,680
Since he shouldn't know anything about you,

80
00:05:06,680 --> 00:05:09,300
I was told never to cause him any trouble.

81
00:05:10,340 --> 00:05:12,680
So at first, I didn't plan to come.

82
00:05:13,580 --> 00:05:16,780
But I wanted to see my dad's face,
just once,

83
00:05:18,820 --> 00:05:20,680
so that's why you came to see me.

84
00:05:21,480 --> 00:05:23,480
Where do you live now?

85
00:05:23,900 --> 00:05:26,380
Are you staying with relatives or somewhere?

86
00:05:26,840 --> 00:05:28,420
I don't have any relatives.

87
00:05:28,860 --> 00:05:30,160
I'm all alone.

88
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:32,200
You live alone?

89
00:05:32,420 --> 00:05:32,780
Yeah.

90
00:05:33,660 --> 00:05:35,800
But I'm not lonely at all.

91
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:39,740
Even living apart,
I know my dad is out there.

92
00:05:39,740 --> 00:05:41,060
I won't accept this.

93
00:05:41,560 --> 00:05:43,160
You keep quiet.

94
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:45,220
Kankichiro,

95
00:05:45,660 --> 00:05:47,320
your mother's name

96
00:05:47,320 --> 00:05:48,320
wouldn't happen to be Akemi?

97
00:05:48,320 --> 00:05:50,240
Or is it Naomi?

98
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:51,900
It's Naomi.

99
00:05:52,920 --> 00:05:54,200
Well, that settles it.

100
00:05:54,960 --> 00:05:56,780
What do you mean, it's settled?

101
00:05:56,780 --> 00:05:58,500
Kankichiro is

102
00:05:58,500 --> 00:06:00,400
your son.

103
00:06:01,080 --> 00:06:01,440
No way...

104
00:06:02,060 --> 00:06:03,400
No, none of that, none of this either.

105
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:04,820
Ten years ago,

106
00:06:04,820 --> 00:06:07,260
"If I could marry Ryo-chan, I'd die happy."

107
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:08,060
and such.

108
00:06:08,580 --> 00:06:11,080
"I want to have Ryo-san's baby," and so on.

109
00:06:11,500 --> 00:06:12,860
Didn't she say that to you?

110
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:14,580
That was a lie, a lie!

111
00:06:14,900 --> 00:06:16,140
Don't you try to wriggle out of it.

112
00:06:16,140 --> 00:06:17,480
Listen, Ryotsu.

113
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:19,680
Now that it's clear you're
really father and son,

114
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:22,760
you can't leave the boy to live alone.

115
00:06:22,760 --> 00:06:26,520
Kankichiro is going to be
raised by you starting today.

116
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:27,580
Mmmmm...

117
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:31,680
Don't be ridiculous! I absolutely refuse!

118
00:06:32,700 --> 00:06:34,160
Now then, Kankishiro-kun.

119
00:06:34,160 --> 00:06:37,280
From now on, you'll live with your dad.

120
00:06:37,280 --> 00:06:38,700
Is that really okay?

121
00:06:41,620 --> 00:06:42,700
Dad!

122
00:06:43,060 --> 00:06:44,100
You little brat!

123
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:44,880
Car!

124
00:06:45,540 --> 00:06:46,060
Ō-chan!

125
00:06:46,360 --> 00:06:47,300
Senpai!

126
00:06:47,440 --> 00:06:48,540
It's the middle of the night!

127
00:06:49,140 --> 00:06:50,280
Dad!

128
00:06:53,160 --> 00:06:54,600
Dad!

129
00:06:57,100 --> 00:06:58,140
Dad!

130
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:05,780
Blood really does tell, doesn't it.

131
00:07:05,780 --> 00:07:06,800
Don't be so naive, Dad!

132
00:07:09,980 --> 00:07:10,540
Damn it!

133
00:07:10,640 --> 00:07:11,080
Dad!

134
00:07:11,660 --> 00:07:12,840
Well, I'm off!

135
00:07:13,160 --> 00:07:13,900
I'm borrowing this!

136
00:07:15,080 --> 00:07:15,780
Ryo-san!

137
00:07:16,080 --> 00:07:16,600
Dad!

138
00:07:20,020 --> 00:07:21,920
Once we're this far, we're home free.

139
00:07:22,380 --> 00:07:24,680
Hey, Kankichi! Stop right there!

140
00:07:27,660 --> 00:07:30,040
What do we do, Kankichi?
Running away is so cowardly!

141
00:07:30,040 --> 00:07:31,340
No, that's not it!

142
00:07:35,640 --> 00:07:37,900
There are so many people, I can't keep up!

143
00:07:37,900 --> 00:07:44,620
Everyone in the shopping street! The man running ahead abandoned
his own child and is fleeing. He's an utterly heartless villain!

144
00:07:44,620 --> 00:07:46,560
Please help us make the arrest!

145
00:07:47,820 --> 00:07:49,680
Don't go making me a criminal on your own!

146
00:07:53,640 --> 00:07:55,240
Get out of the way!

147
00:07:59,720 --> 00:08:23,620
Grrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrr...

148
00:08:23,620 --> 00:08:26,060
There he is! He didn't trip!
Is he coming this way?

149
00:08:26,180 --> 00:08:27,880
So you're bad at pachinko!

150
00:08:28,200 --> 00:08:29,200
Heh-heh, yep!

151
00:08:29,200 --> 00:08:30,260
What are you doing here?

152
00:08:31,060 --> 00:08:33,760
Reiko-san said you'd definitely be here!

153
00:08:34,620 --> 00:08:37,620
That Reiko, always sticking her
nose in where it doesn't belong...

154
00:08:45,940 --> 00:08:48,960
What?! H-hey, move! Let me take over!

155
00:08:49,220 --> 00:08:51,060
No way! It's my turn!

156
00:08:51,060 --> 00:08:53,920
Do you think elementary schoolers
should be playing pachinko?

157
00:08:53,920 --> 00:08:57,940
I might think about it if you stop me.

158
00:08:57,940 --> 00:08:58,860
What?

159
00:08:58,860 --> 00:09:00,480
F-fine.

160
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:02,880
I'll quit for one night, so swap with me.

161
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:04,920
It's 6 o'clock.

162
00:09:05,580 --> 00:09:07,940
Everyone, let's go home.

163
00:09:08,580 --> 00:09:12,480
I never expected everyone to win that much.

164
00:09:12,480 --> 00:09:15,580
Don't forget it's thanks to me, Dad.

165
00:09:15,580 --> 00:09:17,220
Stop calling me Dad.

166
00:09:17,220 --> 00:09:18,440
Call me Ryo-san.

167
00:09:18,440 --> 00:09:19,960
Fine, Dad.

168
00:09:37,420 --> 00:09:40,080
Sorry, sorry, sorry.

169
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:43,040
You cheating wretch, Ryo-sama!

170
00:09:46,880 --> 00:09:48,540
Stop it, big sis!

171
00:09:48,680 --> 00:09:50,480
Mother, you stay out of this!

172
00:09:50,620 --> 00:09:53,500
Miss, are you by any
chance Ryo-san's girlfriend?

173
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:54,860
So what if I am?

174
00:09:55,240 --> 00:09:58,180
Does that mean you'll become my mom someday?

175
00:10:01,260 --> 00:10:02,060
Mom?

176
00:10:07,840 --> 00:10:12,300
What a delightful sound, "Mom."

177
00:10:14,080 --> 00:10:15,020
That's right, indeed.

178
00:10:15,020 --> 00:10:16,960
If you're Ryo-san's child,

179
00:10:16,960 --> 00:10:19,040
then you're as good as my own, aren't you?

180
00:10:19,040 --> 00:10:21,320
What's your name?

181
00:10:21,320 --> 00:10:22,340
Kankichiro.

182
00:10:22,340 --> 00:10:23,920
Kankichiro-kun.

183
00:10:23,920 --> 00:10:27,720
From today, I'll be your mother.

184
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:28,580
Really?

185
00:10:28,580 --> 00:10:30,840
If it's a mom as pretty as you,

186
00:10:30,840 --> 00:10:32,540
I'd be totally happy with that!

187
00:10:32,540 --> 00:10:33,540
How wonderful.

188
00:10:33,540 --> 00:10:36,200
I think we're going to get along well,
don't you?

189
00:10:36,200 --> 00:10:36,680
Yeah.

190
00:10:37,480 --> 00:10:53,860
Nnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnn...

191
00:11:08,980 --> 00:11:12,080
Kankichiro, is my cooking delicious?

192
00:11:12,820 --> 00:11:15,320
Why is Maria barging in too?

193
00:11:15,320 --> 00:11:18,800
Because from today on,
we're family, after all.

194
00:11:18,800 --> 00:11:19,720
Hey.

195
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:27,500
Dad, don't just stay over there.

196
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:29,440
You should just eat with us over here.

197
00:11:29,440 --> 00:11:30,200
Hey.

198
00:11:34,640 --> 00:11:35,800
Hey, Dad.

199
00:11:35,800 --> 00:11:38,620
Let's all go out somewhere tomorrow,
the three of us.

200
00:11:39,260 --> 00:11:40,040
That's right.

201
00:11:40,040 --> 00:11:42,640
Let's have Dad show us around Asakusa,
shall we?

202
00:11:42,640 --> 00:11:43,660
Kankichiro.

203
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:45,780
What are you going on about on your own?

204
00:11:45,780 --> 00:11:47,360
I can't, you know.

205
00:11:47,840 --> 00:11:51,580
And stop calling me "Dad," already.

206
00:11:51,580 --> 00:11:53,960
Kankichiro, have you ever been to Asakusa?

207
00:11:55,280 --> 00:11:57,300
There's an amusement park called Hanayashiki,
you know.

208
00:11:57,300 --> 00:11:59,480
Let's have Dad take us there, shall we?

209
00:11:59,480 --> 00:12:00,640
Yay!

210
00:12:01,120 --> 00:12:03,080
I already told you, I'm not going!

211
00:12:03,080 --> 00:12:06,840
The roller coaster there is really scary.

212
00:12:08,420 --> 00:12:09,540
Looking forward to it

213
00:12:10,180 --> 00:12:13,320
That's great, isn't it, Kankichiro?

214
00:12:13,320 --> 00:12:16,440
Since we're at it,
let's stop by Dad's family home

215
00:12:16,440 --> 00:12:18,980
and show them their grandson's face.

216
00:12:18,980 --> 00:12:20,340
Idiot, what are you talking about?

217
00:12:20,340 --> 00:12:22,740
I told you, I'm not going!

218
00:12:25,360 --> 00:12:28,300
Wow, these lanterns are huge!

219
00:12:28,300 --> 00:12:29,240
Right?

220
00:12:29,780 --> 00:12:31,320
Hurry up, Dad!

221
00:12:31,320 --> 00:12:33,460
I told you, stop calling me Dad!

222
00:12:33,460 --> 00:12:35,640
Stop pulling me!

223
00:12:36,320 --> 00:12:38,940
Hey, Dad, let's buy this!

224
00:12:38,940 --> 00:12:41,140
I already told you not to call me that.

225
00:12:41,140 --> 00:12:42,460
Come on, come on!

226
00:12:42,460 --> 00:12:44,700
Well, stop pulling me already!

227
00:12:46,620 --> 00:12:48,420
Hurry up, hurry!

228
00:12:48,920 --> 00:12:51,140
Go to hell.

229
00:12:51,140 --> 00:12:53,840
Wow, that's amazing!

230
00:13:08,780 --> 00:13:10,140
Dad!

231
00:13:12,040 --> 00:13:14,200
I told you, you're being too persistent!

232
00:13:15,740 --> 00:13:17,400
Try going inside the pachinko machine.

233
00:13:17,400 --> 00:13:20,820
Amazing!

234
00:13:20,820 --> 00:13:22,320
Just as I expected, you're impressive.

235
00:13:23,900 --> 00:13:25,680
Next one, or the one after?

236
00:13:58,660 --> 00:14:00,220
Do you want a bicycle?

237
00:14:00,940 --> 00:14:02,240
I don't want one!

238
00:14:02,240 --> 00:14:04,920
Besides, I can't ride a bike, so there.

239
00:14:04,920 --> 00:14:08,140
What, you can't even ride a bike?

240
00:14:08,140 --> 00:14:09,240
Mind your own business.

241
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:12,180
Alright, I'll teach you to ride one.

242
00:14:12,700 --> 00:14:13,100
Really?

243
00:14:14,360 --> 00:14:17,300
But I'm a strict teacher.

244
00:14:18,900 --> 00:14:21,480
Ryo-san, you can take as many as you like.

245
00:14:28,660 --> 00:14:31,740
Hey, what exactly is Maria?

246
00:14:33,320 --> 00:14:35,880
If you take a bath with her,
you'll see, they say.

247
00:14:36,800 --> 00:14:37,940
Hey, Maria.

248
00:14:37,940 --> 00:14:41,220
Kankichiro says he wants to take a bath with you tonight,
apparently.

249
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:42,520
Sure, that's fine.

250
00:14:42,520 --> 00:14:43,340
Hey.

251
00:14:51,300 --> 00:14:53,300
Kan-chan, how's the water temperature?

252
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:55,800
Yes, it's just right.

253
00:15:13,880 --> 00:15:18,080
To a girl in her prime,

254
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:18,500
Oh -

255
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:20,520
loudly

256
00:15:20,520 --> 00:15:22,920
calling out

257
00:15:22,920 --> 00:15:24,000
and -

258
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:26,000
I-

259
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:26,940
I-

260
00:15:26,940 --> 00:15:27,280
I-

261
00:15:27,280 --> 00:15:27,520
I-

262
00:15:27,520 --> 00:15:27,740
I-

263
00:15:27,740 --> 00:15:27,900
I-

264
00:15:27,900 --> 00:15:28,180
I-

265
00:15:28,180 --> 00:15:28,260
I-

266
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:32,760
I-

267
00:15:39,320 --> 00:15:41,160
Ready -

268
00:15:43,260 --> 00:15:45,260
Dad, you really can do anything

269
00:15:45,680 --> 00:15:47,640
You can tell I'm gonna fall over, right?

270
00:15:49,920 --> 00:15:51,560
Alright, this should be good enough.

271
00:15:52,020 --> 00:15:54,500
Wow, it's like it's brand new!

272
00:15:55,140 --> 00:15:56,840
Then let's get started with the training.

273
00:16:01,720 --> 00:16:04,200
Listen, you only need to pedal lightly.

274
00:16:04,200 --> 00:16:06,220
Keep your balance with the handlebars

275
00:16:06,220 --> 00:16:08,440
and ride all the way
down without falling over.

276
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:09,920
N-no way...

277
00:16:11,160 --> 00:16:13,120
At a park or somewhere, hold the back of it

278
00:16:13,120 --> 00:16:15,640
and gradually teach you to ride,
isn't that how it works?

279
00:16:15,640 --> 00:16:16,480
Don't be spoiled.

280
00:16:16,480 --> 00:16:19,660
What you need in order
to learn to ride a bike

281
00:16:19,660 --> 00:16:22,300
is a sense of balance and courage.

282
00:16:22,300 --> 00:16:29,860
I knew it, this is impossible.

283
00:16:31,940 --> 00:16:33,280
Let's start over.

284
00:16:37,940 --> 00:16:39,360
Again

285
00:16:41,280 --> 00:16:42,440
Again!

286
00:16:43,840 --> 00:16:45,340
Again!

287
00:16:46,340 --> 00:16:47,640
Again!

288
00:16:51,880 --> 00:16:53,000
Again!

289
00:16:58,920 --> 00:16:59,880
I did it!

290
00:17:05,300 --> 00:17:06,820
Now! Pedal!

291
00:17:06,980 --> 00:17:07,720
Y-yes!

292
00:17:07,720 --> 00:17:11,660
Hey! I did it! I can ride! I can ride, Dad!

293
00:17:18,640 --> 00:17:19,040
Are you okay?

294
00:17:20,040 --> 00:17:22,500
Dad, did you see that? I did it!

295
00:17:22,820 --> 00:17:25,960
Yeah. Here, there you go.

296
00:17:34,240 --> 00:17:36,260
Well, shall we head home now?

297
00:17:37,720 --> 00:17:39,520
I'm so hungry.

298
00:17:39,520 --> 00:17:40,300
Okay, okay.

299
00:17:55,620 --> 00:17:57,760
He must have been really tired.

300
00:17:59,520 --> 00:18:00,340
Yeah, I guess so.

301
00:18:01,500 --> 00:18:04,280
Ryo-sama, kids are cute, aren't they?

302
00:18:07,200 --> 00:18:09,900
Maybe having a kid isn't so bad after all.

303
00:18:10,980 --> 00:18:12,420
I-I was joking!

304
00:18:12,420 --> 00:18:13,380
Good night.

305
00:18:24,780 --> 00:18:25,220
No, that's wrong.

306
00:18:26,600 --> 00:18:28,300
You do it like this.

307
00:18:28,920 --> 00:18:29,640
I see.

308
00:18:29,640 --> 00:18:30,400
Like this

309
00:18:30,400 --> 00:18:31,100
Yeah, that's it, that's it.

310
00:18:31,660 --> 00:18:34,040
Ryo-chan,
you're a pretty good dad, aren't you?

311
00:18:35,860 --> 00:18:36,020
Hey!

312
00:18:38,420 --> 00:18:39,880
Isn't this a missing person report?

313
00:18:40,640 --> 00:18:42,200
What's the matter with this?

314
00:18:49,240 --> 00:18:50,640
He was lying, you know.

315
00:18:51,140 --> 00:18:53,840
His parents are supposed
to be coming any moment now.

316
00:18:54,420 --> 00:18:57,120
After he'd finally gotten
close to Ryo-sama too.

317
00:18:57,760 --> 00:18:59,600
I don't know what to say to Ryo-sama.

318
00:19:03,780 --> 00:19:05,920
I've brought Hayato's parents.

319
00:19:06,740 --> 00:19:08,080
Thank you so much for coming.

320
00:19:08,080 --> 00:19:09,940
Sorry for all the trouble.

321
00:19:10,780 --> 00:19:13,020
N-no, well, that is...

322
00:19:13,440 --> 00:19:15,220
I've got him firmly held here.

323
00:19:15,220 --> 00:19:16,380
Hayato!

324
00:19:17,060 --> 00:19:19,520
Hey, Hayato, you worried us sick!

325
00:19:19,520 --> 00:19:22,000
Hayato!

326
00:19:22,660 --> 00:19:23,620
N-no, that's not it!

327
00:19:23,620 --> 00:19:25,180
I'm not Hayato!

328
00:19:25,180 --> 00:19:28,140
Hey, stop lying any more!

329
00:19:30,740 --> 00:19:31,720
Anyway,

330
00:19:33,900 --> 00:19:37,480
Ryo-sama, this child isn't Kankichiro.

331
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:38,480
You...

332
00:19:46,080 --> 00:19:48,120
What on earth happened?

333
00:19:48,600 --> 00:19:49,000
Yes.

334
00:19:50,140 --> 00:19:52,000
It was our fault.

335
00:19:52,500 --> 00:19:56,540
We only recently opened the small
restaurant we'd long wished for.

336
00:19:57,040 --> 00:19:59,740
Yasuraoka-san said she'd
come at three, though.

337
00:20:00,600 --> 00:20:02,260
Then we probably won't finish the prep in time,
will we?

338
00:20:02,260 --> 00:20:05,960
Mom, Kaiko's falling apart.

339
00:20:05,960 --> 00:20:09,020
I can't let go right now.
Keep an eye on Kayato for me.

340
00:20:09,020 --> 00:20:12,540
There, feels good, doesn't it?

341
00:20:23,980 --> 00:20:25,400
Did you bump into something?

342
00:20:26,160 --> 00:20:27,940
Doesn't hurt, doesn't hurt.

343
00:20:27,940 --> 00:20:29,560
Don't cry, you'll make me cry too.

344
00:20:30,600 --> 00:20:31,280
That's not it!

345
00:20:31,440 --> 00:20:34,820
You're the big brother,
so you have to take proper care of him!

346
00:20:37,140 --> 00:20:38,020
A bike?

347
00:20:38,640 --> 00:20:40,319
All my friends have one.

348
00:20:40,369 --> 00:20:42,820
I'm the only one who doesn't have one!

349
00:20:43,280 --> 00:20:47,120
I'll get you one someday. You're in the way of my work. Now run along,
little guy.

350
00:20:47,720 --> 00:20:49,220
You said that the other day too!

351
00:20:50,160 --> 00:20:52,860
Hey, Mom. Buy me a bike.

352
00:20:53,320 --> 00:20:56,360
We don't have that kind of money right now.
Be patient.

353
00:20:56,560 --> 00:20:57,280
But!

354
00:20:57,280 --> 00:20:57,780
Argh!

355
00:20:57,780 --> 00:21:00,620
You're really persistent, aren't you?
No means no.

356
00:21:02,900 --> 00:21:06,760
What's that supposed to mean?! You always
make me do the drum chores and the housework!

357
00:21:07,800 --> 00:21:12,840
Ugh, this is boring! So boring!
Is it really so bad to buy me a bike?!

358
00:21:13,400 --> 00:21:16,600
Hey, you little punk! How dare you
talk back to your parents like that!

359
00:21:17,040 --> 00:21:18,220
I'll smack you, you bastard!

360
00:21:18,780 --> 00:21:19,380
You!

361
00:21:21,660 --> 00:21:24,500
I hate you, Dad and Mom!

362
00:21:24,900 --> 00:21:25,300
Hayato!

363
00:21:29,280 --> 00:21:33,480
I was too busy to think
about how this kid felt.

364
00:21:34,020 --> 00:21:34,420
I see.

365
00:21:35,560 --> 00:21:39,080
But why on earth would he
think Ryotsu was his father?

366
00:21:41,960 --> 00:21:44,540
Sure, I ran away from home,

367
00:21:44,540 --> 00:21:46,620
but I had nowhere to go.

368
00:21:50,580 --> 00:21:53,940
It's not just a flying contest, you know.

369
00:21:53,940 --> 00:21:57,440
You have to calculate the wind direction
and catch the air current, right?

370
00:21:57,940 --> 00:22:00,700
A north-northwest wind.

371
00:22:00,700 --> 00:22:04,060
And seeing Ryo-san playing
happily with the kids,

372
00:22:04,060 --> 00:22:06,560
busted.

373
00:22:06,560 --> 00:22:10,480
I wished my dad was a guy like Ryo-san.

374
00:22:11,620 --> 00:22:12,580
So that's how it was.

375
00:22:13,100 --> 00:22:15,420
Sorry for yelling at you, Dad.

376
00:22:15,420 --> 00:22:16,160
Hayato.

377
00:22:16,160 --> 00:22:18,240
Come on, let's go home, Hayato.

378
00:22:19,980 --> 00:22:20,700
I don't want to!

379
00:22:21,520 --> 00:22:23,600
I want to live with Ryo-san!

380
00:22:23,940 --> 00:22:24,400
Hayato!

381
00:22:25,060 --> 00:22:27,820
When I get home, I'll be all alone again!

382
00:22:28,260 --> 00:22:30,800
Ryo-san even takes me to the amusement park,

383
00:22:31,220 --> 00:22:33,420
and he even teaches me how to ride a bike!

384
00:22:33,920 --> 00:22:36,860
Hey, Ryo-san, let me stay at your place!

385
00:22:37,280 --> 00:22:40,240
Let's all live happily together again,
the three of us with Maria!

386
00:22:40,580 --> 00:22:41,360
Calm down!

387
00:22:43,560 --> 00:22:45,820
Who'd ever live with a brat like you!

388
00:22:46,960 --> 00:22:47,800
Ryo-san...

389
00:22:47,800 --> 00:22:50,640
I hate liars and caterpillars!

390
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:54,660
Ryo-san, I'm sorry. I won't lie anymore.

391
00:22:54,660 --> 00:22:55,200
Don't be so persistent.

392
00:22:57,280 --> 00:22:58,180
Ryo-san

393
00:22:58,700 --> 00:23:01,280
I never want to see your face again!

394
00:23:02,440 --> 00:23:03,440
Just go home already!

395
00:23:04,880 --> 00:23:05,620
Ryotsu

396
00:23:12,180 --> 00:23:14,380
Thank you so much for all your trouble.

397
00:23:14,900 --> 00:23:15,220
Thank you very much.

398
00:23:16,740 --> 00:23:18,440
Well, take care, Hayato.

399
00:23:18,820 --> 00:23:20,320
Come visit us again sometime.

400
00:23:20,680 --> 00:23:21,580
Come by anytime.

401
00:23:22,020 --> 00:23:24,420
No more lying, Kankichiro.

402
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:30,360
Well, shall we go, Hayato?

403
00:23:30,700 --> 00:23:31,400
Kankichiro.

404
00:23:33,240 --> 00:23:34,940
Take the bike out front with you.

405
00:23:34,940 --> 00:23:36,900
Really? Is that okay?

406
00:23:37,440 --> 00:23:40,200
Leaving something like that
here would just get in the way.

407
00:23:41,100 --> 00:23:43,220
It's a full custom order I built myself,
after all.

408
00:23:43,220 --> 00:23:44,520
Ride it carefully.

409
00:23:50,240 --> 00:23:50,900
Ryo-san!

410
00:23:51,220 --> 00:23:55,100
I'll learn to ride a
bike as well as Ryo-san!

411
00:23:56,220 --> 00:23:58,140
See you, Kankichiro!

412
00:24:01,340 --> 00:24:05,560
Kicking the alarm clock,
my little toe hurts, ouch!

413
00:24:07,680 --> 00:24:13,940
Quickly draw on my eyebrows,
then dash to the station, dash, dash, dash.

414
00:24:13,940 --> 00:24:19,560
Every train, pressed against some old man's back,
one loop around.

415
00:24:20,560 --> 00:24:25,880
Another hard week,
unreasonable demands are only natural.

416
00:24:27,060 --> 00:24:33,400
Though I act cool with one hand,
it's beef bowl with extra broth.

417
00:24:33,400 --> 00:24:40,280
Overtime-streak irritation,
cleared away with more irritation.

418
00:24:43,500 --> 00:24:50,060
Every day is no problem,
once I step through a hot shower.

419
00:24:50,060 --> 00:24:56,580
Every day is no problem,
recovering my energy with a sleep pillow.

420
00:24:59,740 --> 00:25:06,220
Every day is no problem,
I love myself just like this.

421
00:25:06,720 --> 00:25:09,380
Every day is no-problem-brave.

422
00:25:09,380 --> 00:25:13,060
Monday, with hearts flying all around.

423
00:25:20,580 --> 00:25:22,060
A charity bazaar?

424
00:25:22,200 --> 00:25:26,120
Someone who makes money off a business
doesn't strike me as the donating type.

425
00:25:26,120 --> 00:25:29,660
What? I never said anyone
would buy my collection!

426
00:25:29,660 --> 00:25:31,160
Don't be an idiot, Komaji!

427
00:25:31,160 --> 00:25:33,740
Then let's settle it with a bazaar showdown,
me versus you!

428
00:25:33,740 --> 00:25:37,520
Next time, the charity bazaar clash,
see you there!

429
00:25:38,500 --> 00:25:40,820
That place is Kameari!

430
00:25:41,760 --> 00:25:44,720
Well, it's surely Kameari!

431
00:25:44,720 --> 00:25:49,160
Everyone, come on over to our town!

432
00:25:50,260 --> 00:25:50,780
Thank you.

